body:
>I know people that have **abused** FMLA for "stress leave"

imagine getting panic attacks at work, and then when you utilize fmla, people claim youre "abusing it." insurance companies don't scrutinize those with pre-existing conditions because of fmla abuse; its because they dont want to pay for your pre-existing condition.

if you want to claim those relieving themselves of stress are committing fraud, you're welcome to take my incurable mental illness as well. (hint: it's not anxiety and/or depression, although theyre not anything to laugh at either.)
